WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.699
Your own return - ITR-1, 2, 3 or 4, for yourself or a family HUF. Start from your documents: {product} reads them, checks them against each other, works out both regimes and makes the department's JSON.

2
00:00:17.297 --> 00:00:27.617
Gather, check, choose, review, file. Each step ticks itself off as it is done, and you can click any step to go back to it.

3
00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:46.355
No client to add first. Drop the pre-filled JSON or a return already filed, and the person - or the HUF - is made from it: PAN, name, date of birth. A CA firm sees its people here; you go straight to your own return.

4
00:00:46.952 --> 00:00:54.392
A checklist of what to have before you start. Each line ticks itself when the document is in.

5
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:11.219
Who issues each document and what it gives your return: Form 16 from your employer; the AIS, TIS and 26AS from the department; a capital-gains statement from CAMS or your broker; your bank statement.

6
00:01:11.827 --> 00:01:29.157
PDF, Excel, CSV or JSON: the pre-filled JSON, Form 16 from each employer, the AIS, TIS and 26AS, a CAMS or broker statement, a bank statement, last year's filed return.

7
00:01:29.766 --> 00:01:40.546
An AIS or 26AS PDF opens with its password - your PAN in small letters and your date of birth. The eye shows what you typed.

8
00:01:41.156 --> 00:02:09.496
Every document shows what was read from it - salary, tax deducted, interest, each sale - and, if you do not have it yet, how to get it. Drop the same kind again and you are asked first: replace it, or keep both. A second Form 16 from the same employer is asked about too - a revised one replaces the first; one from another employer is a job change, and both count.

9
00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:19.930
Every figure you change and every document you replace is in History, with who and when. Old versions are kept, ready to download.

10
00:02:20.531 --> 00:02:28.791
Total income, tax, and the refund due or the amount to pay - kept up to date with every document and every figure.

11
00:02:29.406 --> 00:02:48.866
Form 16's tax deducted beside 26AS, and salary and interest beside the AIS. Two employers in a year? Each took off the standard deduction - the return takes it once, and the check says so. A gap is shown to you before the department finds it.

12
00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:57.648
Both regimes worked out in full, the cheaper one marked. Pick either - the other stays one click away.

13
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:05.860
Gross income, what is exempt, the deductions, the taxable income and the tax - step by step.

14
00:03:06.468 --> 00:03:16.288
Each employer's figures from Form 16, with the source beside them. Type over anything - your own figure is marked as yours.

15
00:03:16.906 --> 00:03:26.216
Days in India this year and the years before decide resident, not ordinarily resident or non-resident - and so which income counts.

16
00:03:26.827 --> 00:03:40.797
Arrears for an earlier year: each year's income and regime, and the relief under section 89 worked out, with a reminder to file Form 10E - even for a year over fifty lakh, with that year's surcharge.

17
00:03:41.406 --> 00:03:51.176
Foreign salary, interest or rent, by country, with the tax paid there - relief under the treaty, or section 91 without one.

18
00:03:51.797 --> 00:04:02.017
A resident's bank accounts, shares and property abroad, accounts you can sign for, trusts and other income from outside India - for Schedule FA.

19
00:04:02.625 --> 00:04:09.965
Your spouse's or minor child's income that the law adds to yours - with the exemption for each child.

20
00:04:10.577 --> 00:04:23.367
Self-occupied or let out, rent, municipal tax and loan interest. A co-owned house is taken by your share, and interest before the house was finished in five parts.

21
00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:56.178
Presumptive income under 44AD, 44ADA or 44AE, or your own profit and loss. Receipts can come from your bank statement. Cash received and paid decide the tax-audit limit; left 44AD in the last five years, and it stays closed. GST turnover per GSTIN, typed or read from your GSTR-3B. The form follows: ITR-4, or ITR-3.

22
00:04:56.781 --> 00:05:04.001
Savings and deposit interest, dividends, family pension - from the AIS, or typed.

23
00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:14.830
Lottery and online games, and crypto or other virtual digital assets - taxed at thirty percent, a crypto loss set off against nothing.

24
00:05:15.452 --> 00:05:23.682
Advance tax and self-assessment tax, with the BSR code and challan number - or read from the AIS.

25
00:05:24.297 --> 00:05:46.997
Every sale from a CAMS or broker statement, or typed: shares and funds with grandfathering, and a house or land with the cheaper of the two rates. Exemptions under 54, 54EC and 54F - more than one on a sale, each checked against its time limit. A CAMS or KFintech PDF is read too.

26
00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:57.210
Losses from earlier years, set off this year and carried on - or filled from last year's filed ITR-2 or ITR-3.

27
00:05:57.827 --> 00:06:07.137
Gifts of money or property: from a relative or on your wedding they are free; from others, over fifty thousand in a year is income.

28
00:06:07.735 --> 00:06:22.835
80C to 80G, and more for the old regime: 80DD, 80DDB, 80EE, 80EEA, 80EEB, 80GG and 80GGC, with the details each schedule asks for.

29
00:06:23.437 --> 00:06:30.277
Contact details for the return, farm income, and for an HUF the Karta who signs it.

30
00:06:30.906 --> 00:06:38.826
Once filed, note the date and acknowledgement - and compare what was filed with what {product} worked out.

31
00:06:39.452 --> 00:06:49.272
Download the department's JSON for ITR-1, 2, 3 or 4, checked against its schema, and upload it on the e-filing portal.

32
00:06:49.891 --> 00:07:07.121
Missed something in an earlier year? The updated return, ITR-U: the extra tax, interest and the additional tax worked out at that year's rates - capital gains, surcharge and interest for each instalment - and whether you can file one at all.
